== Introduction
<introduction>
This special weekend session covers practical rulings of #strong[Eid
al-Aḍḥā] and #strong[Qurbānī (Uḍḥiyah)] based on the short kitāb
#emph[Aḥkām e Eid al-Aḍḥā wa Qurbānī] by the late #strong[Muftī Muḥammad
Shafīʿ ʿUthmānī] (raḥimahullāh), former Grand Muftī of Pakistan. The
goal is to revise and refresh these masāʾil before the blessed days
begin.

#horizontalrule

== Faḍāʾil: Virtues of the First Ten Days of Dhul Ḥijjah
<fa-a-il-virtues-of-the-first-ten-days-of-dhul-hijjah>
The first ten days of Dhul Ḥijjah are the #strong[best days of the
entire Islamic calendar] (after Ramaḍān). Allah has taken an oath in
their name:

#quote(block: true)[
وَالْفَجْرِ وَلَيَالٍ عَشْرٍ

#emph["By the dawn, and by the ten nights."]

#strong[Ref:] Sūrah al-Fajr (89:1--2)
]

Whenever Allah takes an oath by something, it indicates its immense
value.

#strong[Key virtues (from aḥādīth as cited in class):] - One fast during
these ten days equals the reward of #strong[one year] of fasting. - The
ʿibādah of one night among these ten nights equals the reward of
#strong[Laylat al-Qadr]. - The #strong[9th of Dhul Ḥijjah] (Yawm
al-ʿArafah) is the most special: fasting on it expiates sins of
#strong[one year before and one year after]. - The night between the 9th
and 10th is the best of these nights.

#horizontalrule

=== Recommended: Not Cutting Nails and Hair
<recommended-not-cutting-nails-and-hair>
A person who intends to slaughter an animal should #strong[not cut their
nails or hair] during these ten days --- resembling one in the state of
#strong[iḥrām]. This is a recommended practice (mustaḥabb), not
obligatory.

#strong[Practical advice:] - Trim nails and settle hair #strong[before]
the ten days begin. - If nails or hair become unsightly or cause
difficulty (e.g., moustache interfering with eating), they #strong[may
be cut] --- removing harm takes priority over gaining the benefit of a
recommended act.

#strong[For those sending Qurbānī abroad:] If the Qurbānī is performed
in another country where Eid is one day later, the person should wait
until the slaughter is done there before cutting nails/hair, to achieve
this sunnah fully.

#horizontalrule

== Takbīr al-Tashrīq
<takbir-al-tashriq>
It is #strong[wājib] to recite the Takbīr al-Tashrīq after every
#strong[farḍ ṣalāh] from the #strong[Fajr of the 9th of Dhul Ḥijjah] to
the #strong[ʿAṣr of the 13th of Dhul Ḥijjah] --- spanning five days and
twenty-three prayers.

- Obligatory on #strong[both men and women], whether praying with
  jamāʿah or alone.
- #strong[Men] recite it audibly (not excessively loud --- just
  audible).
- #strong[Women] recite it quietly.
- It is recited #strong[once] after each farḍ prayer.

#horizontalrule

== Sunan of Eid Day
<sunan-of-eid-day>
The following acts are #strong[mustaḥabb/masnūn] on the day of Eid
al-Aḍḥā:

+ #strong[Waking up early] in the morning.
+ #strong[Taking a bath (ghusl).]
+ #strong[Using miswāk.]
+ #strong[Wearing the best available clothing] --- not necessarily
  expensive; just the best one has.
+ #strong[Applying perfume (ʿiṭr).]
+ #strong[Not eating before the Eid prayer] --- the first thing to eat
  should be the #strong[uḍḥiyah meat] (the meat from one's sacrifice).
  This is the "hospitality from Allah's side." This is recommended, not
  obligatory.
+ #strong[Reciting takbīr (Allāhu Akbar)] while walking to the muṣallā
  --- in a moderate voice, not silent and not excessively loud.

#horizontalrule

== Eid Prayer --- Key Rulings
<eid-prayer-key-rulings>
The Eid prayer is #strong[wājib]. It has a specific methodology with
#strong[six additional takbīrāt]:

- #strong[First rakʿah:] Three extra takbīrāt #strong[before] the
  qirāʾah.
- #strong[Second rakʿah:] Three extra takbīrāt #strong[after] the
  qirāʾah.
- In each takbīr, raise the hands and let them drop --- #strong[except]
  the third takbīr of the first rakʿah, because qirāʾah follows it
  (hands remain folded for qirāʾah).

#strong[Easy way to remember:] 3 before (first rakʿah), 3 after (second
rakʿah). Raise and drop hands each time, except the one before qirāʾah.

#strong[If the Imām misses the takbīrāt:] No sajdah sahw is performed.
The reason: it is a large gathering, and performing sajdah sahw could
create confusion and fitnah among people who lack detailed knowledge of
these rulings.

#strong[Khuṭbah after Eid prayer:] It is #strong[masnūn] to listen to
the khuṭbah. One should not leave or get engaged in other activities.

#horizontalrule

== Qurbānī (Uḍḥiyah) --- The Slaughtering
<qurbani-u-hiyah-the-slaughtering>
=== Status and Virtues
<status-and-virtues>
Qurbānī is one of the greatest acts of ʿibādah during these days. No
deed is more beloved to Allah on these days than the slaughtering.

It is a remembrance of the #strong[Sunnah of Ibrāhīm] (ʿalayhi
al-salām), who was commanded to sacrifice his son in a dream and
proceeded to obey.

#strong[Virtues from ḥadīth (as cited in class):] - In exchange of every
#strong[hair] of the animal, there is one reward. If the animal has
wool, every strand of wool carries a reward. - The person is
#strong[forgiven] before the first drop of blood falls on the ground ---
provided the intention is sincere.

=== Ruling --- Wājib or Sunnah?
<ruling-wajib-or-sunnah>
